To whom it may concern,     I am unable to use the proxy ip through the Python requests library. I get the following error when I run this code:      import requests
     proxies = {
    "https": "https://MY_USERNAME:MY_PASSWORD@us-west-shield-01.quotaguard.com:9294",
}
     res = requests.get("https://ip.quotaguard.com/", proxies = proxies)
     print(res.text)  ProxyError: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='ip.quotaguard.com', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by ProxyError('Cannot connect to proxy.', ConnectionResetError(10054, 'An existing connection was forcibly closed by the remote host', None, 10054, None)))     We have been able to connect using pycurl, but we need to be able to connect using the requests library.      I hope you have a solution!      Thank you.

Hello,

I've applied the following code to my React application and need assistance
getting the static IP to work properly. I need the static IP to serve the
entire application.

'use strict';
require('dotenv').config({ silent: true });

var testEndpoint = 'https://synaptent-surveyjs.herokuapp.com';
var proxy = process.env.QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL;
var agent = new HttpsProxyAgent(proxy);
var options = {
  uri: url.parse(testEndpoint),
  agent
};

function callback(error, response, body) {
  if (!error && response.statusCode == 200) {
    console.log('body: ', body);
  } else {
    console.log('error: ', error);
  }
}

request(options, callback);

Please let me know what I am doing wrong. The application compiles fine,
but is not at the static IP. Maybe I simply don't have a thorough
understanding of how this is supposed to work. Please bear with me.

Thank you,

Helen

Hello,

I just signed up QG shield (though static might be sufficient).  I’ve tried both locally and an AWS API gateway deployed version with SSL to make a simple proxy request and both are timing out.  Here’s the error:

requests.exceptions.ProxyError: HTTPConnectionPool(host='us-east-shield-01.quotaguard.com', port=9294): Max retries exceeded with url: http://ip.quotaguard.com/ (Caused by ProxyError('Cannot connect to proxy.', RemoteDisconnected('Remote end closed connection without response')))

And the code:
@app.route('/')
def index():
    proxies = {
        "http": os.environ['QUOTAGUARD_URL']
    }
    res = requests.get("http://ip.quotaguard.com/", proxies=proxies)

    return {'version': 1.2, 'ip': res.text}

Also, I’ve set up the account to have static IPs for my API gateway code.  Not sure if you have specific information for API Gateway/Lambda, but that would be helpful.

Note the account we’re using is registered under 'katence@givevolunteers.org’

Thank you,

Alan

Hello!

My company is interested in using Qutoaguard Shield to proxy our AWS RDS
MySQL connections from our heroku servers in order to whitelist
communications.
It's mission critical for us to maintain encryption throughout the entire
line of communication.
We use Node for our servers. Our following code doesn't seem to establish a
connection with our MySQL servers due to some incorrect SSL configuration.
Can you please let us know if we're doing something wrong (see code below)?
We're trying to force SSL throughout the entire line of communication. We
are passing the AWS CA in mysql_server_options to establish a sock
connection to the remote database. Our database has force_ssl enabled.

Thanks so much!
Best,
Marc

const url = require('url');
const SocksConnection = require('socksjs');

// SOCKS Proxy for fixed IP
const proxy = url.parse(QUOTA_GUARD_URL);
const auth = proxy.auth;
const username = auth.split(':')[0];
const pass = auth.split(':')[1];

const socks_options = {
host: proxy.hostname,
port: 1080,
user: username,
pass,
};

const mysql_server_options = {
host: process.env.DB_MYSQL_HOST,
port: process.env.DB_MYSQL_PORT,
user: process.env.DB_MYSQL_USER,
password: process.env.DB_MYSQL_PASSWORD,
database: process.env.DB_MYSQL_DB,
ssl: {
ca,
},
};

module.exports = () => {
return new SocksConnection(mysql_server_options, socks_options);
};

Hi, we're running QuotaGuard Static on Heroku and using it to connect to a database.  We've just started seeing this error in the logs:   2020-01-27T14:58:55.217244+00:00 app[web.1]: 2020/01/27 14:58:55 Unable to dial signal-datomic-staging.cervest.com:443: proxy: SOCKS5 proxy at eu-west-static-02.quotaguard.com:1080 rejected username/password.  This happens in Review Apps, which have the QUOTAGUARD_STATIC_URL injected by QuotaGuard, and that URL contains the username/password in question.       We have the following in our app.json:       "addons": [
      {
        "plan": "quotaguardstatic:starter",
        "options": {
          "proxy": "eu-west-static-02"
        }
      }
    ],     Has anything changed?  Do you know why we've just started seeing this now?  What should we do to fix it?     Thanks,     Conan

Hi,

I tried using QuotaGuard Shield in my Heroku PHP application but could not get it working with the following code snippet from your documentation (https://devcenter.heroku.com/articles/quotaguardshield#https-proxy-with-php):

<?php

function lookup() {
  $quotaguard_env = getenv("QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL");
  $quotaguard = parse_url($quotaguard_env);

  $proxyUrl = $quotaguard['host'].":".$quotaguard['port'];
  $proxyAuth = $quotaguard['user'].":".$quotaguard['pass'];

  $url = "https://ip.quotaguard.com/";

  $ch = curl_init();
  curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_URL, $url);
  curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, 1);
  curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_PROXY, $proxyUrl);
  curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_PROXYAUTH, CURLAUTH_BASIC);
  curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_PROXYUSERPWD, $proxyAuth);
  $response = curl_exec($ch);
  return $response;
}

$res = lookup();
print_r($res);

?>

It results in a 504 Gateway Timeout error, and nothing get logged into the dashboard. After some searching, the problem seems to be that the cURL option CURLOPT_PROXYTYPE is set by default to CURLPROXY_HTTP, but it should be set to CURLPROXY_HTTPS, because QuotaGuard Shield uses a HTTPS (not HTTP) proxy. The same code snippet probably works fine in QuotaGuard Static, because it uses a HTTP (not HTTPS) proxy.

In other words, you have to add the following line into the code snippet: curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_PROXYTYPE, CURLPROXY_HTTPS);

After that, everything seems to work fine.

In order to avoid other potential users from running into the same problem, I would strongly recommend updating the code snippet as soon as possible. Could you also confirm that it is otherwise valid and up-to-date for QuotaGuard Shield and that no other changes are required in comparison to QuotaGuard Static?

Best regards,

Markus Makkonen
Postdoctoral Researcher, D.Sc. (Econ.)
 
University of Jyväskylä
Faculty of Information Technology
Agora C419.2
 
Office: +358 40 805 4292
Mobile: +358 40 523 0575
E-mail: markus.v.makkonen@jyu.fi

